//! The SANSOS text kernel.
//!
//! Everything above this crate — the assembler's tokenizer, the terminal's cell
//! model, the shaper, the linker's symbol table — depends on agreeing what a
//! character *is*. See `research/01-sanskrit-computing-foundations.md`.
//!
//! Tables in [`tables`] are generated by `cargo run -p ucdgen` from the pinned
//! UCD; they are checked in so that building SANSOS needs no network.

//! `normalize` needs an allocator; segmentation (task `A-014`) must stay
//! allocation-free so the terminal line discipline can use it (doc 04 §3).
#![no_std]
// Enforced, not asserted. The fuzz targets run without AddressSanitizer,
// because ASan's runtime traps on this host before `main` (see
// `tools/check-fuzz.sh`). That is only acceptable while this crate has no
// `unsafe` in it: safe Rust's memory errors are panics, and libFuzzer catches
// panics unaided. Removing this line removes the fuzzing argument with it.
#![forbid(unsafe_code)]

